1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,122
Two more animals to meet: the Owl and the Beaver.

2
00:00:04,133 --> 00:00:05,327
This is the Owl.

3
00:00:05,647 --> 00:00:07,119
The Owl loves pairs.

4
00:00:07,439 --> 00:00:09,701
A pair is two stones of the same color.

5
00:00:11,583 --> 00:00:12,863
One white stone.

6
00:00:13,183 --> 00:00:15,081
Not a pair yet, so no points.

7
00:00:16,949 --> 00:00:18,443
A second white stone.

8
00:00:18,763 --> 00:00:19,765
That's a pair!

9
00:00:20,085 --> 00:00:21,109
Four points.

10
00:00:23,183 --> 00:00:24,975
Another pair, red this time.

11
00:00:25,295 --> 00:00:26,489
Four more points.

12
00:00:27,599 --> 00:00:28,965
This is the Beaver.

13
00:00:29,285 --> 00:00:30,906
The Beaver wants two groups.

14
00:00:33,183 --> 00:00:35,572
On top: three stones of one color.

15
00:00:35,892 --> 00:00:37,705
Three blues make five points.

16
00:00:39,783 --> 00:00:41,916
Below: two stones of one color.

17
00:00:42,236 --> 00:00:43,900
Two yellows make two points.

18
00:00:45,033 --> 00:00:46,292
Both groups done?

19
00:00:46,612 --> 00:00:47,486
Bonus!

20
00:00:47,806 --> 00:00:49,129
Seven more points.

21
00:00:49,449 --> 00:00:50,857
That's fourteen in all.

22
00:00:51,966 --> 00:00:54,014
Here are all five animals together.

23
00:00:54,334 --> 00:00:55,934
Each one has its own rule.

24
00:00:57,066 --> 00:00:57,962
Remember.

25
00:00:58,282 --> 00:01:01,653
The Owl wants pairs of the same color, four points each.

26
00:01:01,973 --> 00:01:04,661
The Beaver wants three the same, plus two the same.

27
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,794
Finish both, and get a bonus.

28
00:01:07,114 --> 00:01:09,183
Next: how to get your cards back.
